# Engine promotion gate (frozen architecture)

Downpour Trade AI is a **deterministic** intelligence platform. The lane → regime → synthesizer → risk → calibration split is **frozen**. Do not grow indicator count or add parallel scoring systems without research promotion.

## Pipeline (required for any scoring change)

```
Research → Experiment → Walk-forward → Calibration impact → Production config
```

Follow **`Research_Roadmap.md`** for experiment design. Never: Idea → Implementation → Synthesizer.

## No feature enters the synthesizer unless ALL are true

- **Deterministic** — Same inputs (bar snapshot + config hash) → same scores and verdict; no LLM, randomness, or wall-clock in the hot path.
- **Reproducible** — Documented rule with evidence strings; replay-compatible.
- **Historical data available** — Backtest can apply the rule on `df.iloc[:i+1]` or on a **versioned feature snapshot** with the same semantics; otherwise **Context / Evidence / Trust only** (see `docs/BACKTEST_FIDELITY.md`).
- **Walk-forward tested** — Compared to baseline **B0**; OOS PF and WF acceptance criteria in `Research_Roadmap.md` §2.
- **Calibration improved or neutral** — Bucket monotonicity and OOS trade count gates; must not degrade WF pass without documented trade-off.
- **Statistically justified** — Practical gates in Research Roadmap (not “felt good”).
- **Explainable** — Every score change has `evidence[]` lines; no opaque composites.
- **Replay compatible** — Appears in replay timeline or lane evidence when relevant.

If any check fails → **Reject**, or promote as **Evidence (P1)**, **Regime modifier (P2)**, or **Confidence modifier (P3)** only—**not** lane score.

## Architecture boundaries (do not blur)

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| **Engine lanes** | Technical, Structure, Flow — scored features only after promotion |
| **Regime** | Tradeability, weights, optional warnings—not duplicate synthesizers |
| **Synthesizer** | Alignment, thresholds, NO_TRADE default |
| **Risk** | SL/TP/size; reads structure levels, does not invent signals |
| **Calibration / Trust** | Buckets, WF, confidence labels |
| **Context** | News, ETF, macro, whales—**never** feed synthesizer unless promoted via research |
| **UI / API enrich** | Projection and display only; no hidden scoring |

## Single ownership

Every capability has **one owner lane or layer** (see `Quant_Architecture_Blueprint.md` §5). Do not duplicate logic across Flow, Structure, and Risk.

## Preferred actions

- **Simplify** correlated signals (e.g. technical orthogonalization) before adding new indicators.
- **Extend** existing lanes; use `structure_events` for evidence-only patterns.
- **Version** config and calibration artifacts (`config_hash`, `calibration_id`) when promotion lands.

## Reject without discussion

- LLM or NLP **scores** in engine paths
- Narrative/news/social **lane scores**
- Duplicate indicators (e.g. EMA 9/21 alongside 20/50) without **replacing** correlated terms and a passed **R0** experiment
- Parallel “strategy builder” or second synthesizer
- Features that competitors ship but fail reproducibility or WF

